# pnpm Workspaces Management

This repository uses **pnpm workspaces** to manage multiple packages. Follow these guidelines to maintain consistency and efficiency.

## Workspace Structure

```
step-nc/
├── packages/
│   └── <package-name>/ # Package in of workspace project
├── pnpm-workspace.yaml
└── package.json       # Workspace scripts
```

## Essential Commands

### Installation and Dependencies

```bash
# Install all workspace dependencies
pnpm install

# Install dependency in a specific package
pnpm --filter <package-name> add <dependency>

# Install dependency in all packages
pnpm -r add <dependency> -D

# Install dependency only in root
pnpm add <dependency> -D --ignore-workspace
```

### Script Execution

```bash
# Run script in all packages
pnpm -r <script>

# Run script in specific package
pnpm --filter <package-name> <script>

# Common workspace scripts:
pnpm build      # Build all packages
pnpm clean      # Clean builds
pnpm dev        # Development mode
pnpm test       # Run tests
pnpm lint       # Linting
pnpm typecheck  # Type checking
```

## Package Management

### Create New Package

```bash
# 1. Create directory
mkdir packages/<new-package>

# 2. Initialize package.json
cd packages/<new-package>
pnpm init

# 3. Configure build (tsup recommended)
# Check configuration in existing packages
```

### Inter-Package Dependencies

```json
// In packages/A/package.json
{
  "dependencies": {
    "@step-nc/<package-name>": "workspace:*"
  }
}
```

### Publishing

We use **changesets** for versioning:

```bash
# Create changeset for changes
pnpm changeset

# Version packages
pnpm version-packages

# Publish
pnpm release
```

